# No em dashes in copy

Do not use em dashes (`—`) anywhere in user-facing site content, including case studies, captions, quotes, meta copy, and comments that describe visible text.

Do not replace em dashes with hyphens (`-`). Rewrite the sentence with clearer punctuation instead.

## Preferred replacements

| Use case | Instead of | Prefer |
|----------|------------|--------|
| Parenthetical aside | `weak—a baseline CTR—and` | `weak, with a baseline CTR around 0.29%, and` |
| Appositive | `carousel—a modern format` | `carousel, a modern format` |
| List or definition | `content—premium tiles` | `content: premium tiles` |
| Caption label | `hero—legacy banner` | `hero: legacy banner` |
| Quote / speech | `ads—I ignore them` | `ads, so I ignore them` |
| Clarifying detail | `UI—slot placement` | `UI, including slot placement` |

## Examples

```
❌ engagement was weak—a baseline CTR around 0.29%—and they couldn't
✅ engagement was weak, with a baseline CTR around 0.29%, and they couldn't

❌ 84 participants—casual, power, and browser personas—to validate
✅ 84 participants (casual, power, and browser personas) to validate

❌ Collection Ads hero - legacy GAM banner
✅ Collection Ads hero: legacy GAM banner
```

En dashes in numeric ranges (e.g. `1–3`, `4–9`, `2023–2025`) are fine when they denote a span.
